","PETITIONER was sent to prison for four years and fined five thousand taka by a special tribunal in Khulna for an offence under the special powers statute, in a case arising out of a police station case of 2008 at Batiaghata. He appealed and was enlarged on bail for six months at the admission stage, and no step was taken afterwards, so the bail ran out in November 2015. RESPONDENT is the state. He appeals against the conviction and sentence, contending that they cannot be sustained on the record.",Special Powers Act 1974,REFUSED,"The court noted that the appeal had been pending for more than nine years and had come up in the list with the name of the appellant's advocate for many days without anyone appearing to press it. The ad interim bail of six months had expired in November 2015 and there had been no attempt to have it extended. In those circumstances the appellant was held to be a fugitive from law and justice, and the court declined to act in aid of such a person, following the Appellate Division. The appeal failed, and he was given three months to surrender his bail bond.",5c38b6830319a76eb7e0077de1c8e4d0e7d24b61701c6d33a32642cc6d5dcae3
