Pursuant thereto the respondent No.7 having deposited the required 
amount of lease money for the respective year the Revenue Deputy 
Collector, Pabna and Member Secretary of District Jolmohal Management 
Committee vide Memo dated 17.01.2024 (Annexure-8 of the 
supplementary affidavit to the affidavit-in-opposition) directed the 
Assistant Commissioner (Land), Chatmohor, Pabna to submit report 
subject to handing over possession of the said “Jolmohal”. On the same 
date i.e. on 17.01.2024 a lease deed was also executed between the 
respondent No.7 and the concerned Additional Deputy Commissioner 
(Revenue), Pabna, (Annexure-8A of the supplementary affidavit to the 
affidavit-in-opposition).  
 However, challenging the impugned decision of the respondent 
No.1 i.e. Ministry of Land to give lease of the respective “Jalmohal” in 
favour of the respondent No.7 the petitioner Samity filed the instant writ 
petition and obtained the present Rule Nisi along with an order of stay of 
the impugned order dated 04.01.2024 (Annexure-A).  
Being aggrieved with the interim order of stay the respondent No.7 
moved before the Hon’ble Appellate Division by filing Civil Petition to 
Leave to Appeal No. 389 of 2024. The Appellate Division upon hearing 
the respective contending parties without interfering with the interim 
order of stay vide order dated 04.03.2024 directed this Bench to hear and 
dispose of the Rule on merit.  
Respondent No.7 entered appearance by filing affidavit-in-
opposition and supplementary affidavit to the affidavit-in-opposition 
stating inter alia, that respondent No.7 is a registered Samity namely 
“Uttar Sengram Natabaria Khalifapara Matshazibi Shamobay Samity

<<PAGE 5>>

5
Ltd.” under Somobay Samity Ain, 2001 (as ameded in 2002 and 2013 
respectively) and Samobay Samity Bidimala, 2004. Said samity is 
actively working in due compliance of law. To that effect, the Upazila 
Somobay Officer, Chartmoha, Pabna issued two separate certificates 
dated 07.01.2021 and 15.10.2023 respectively in favour of the respondent 
Samity.  
The Mayor of Chatmohar Pourashova, Pabna and Member No.1 of 
Bilchalon Union Parishad, Upazilla-Pabna issued respective certificates 
dated 28.02.2024, 21.02.2024 and 26.02.2024 respectively stating that all 
the members of the respondent No.7 were fishermen although they did not 
get Fisherman ID Card from the Department of Fisheries till date. 
 In this regard, however, it has been stated that the fisherman 
registration for getting Fisherman ID Card is a continuous process and 
thus, the Senior Upazila Fisheries Officer, Chatmohar, Pabna had issued 
certificates from 11.09.2023 to 20.02.2024 certifying the respective names 
who were holding Fisherman ID Card. However, during this time four 
members of the respondent No.7, Samity had obtained Fisherman ID Card 
and that rest of the applications are still pending for issuance of the said 
cards.  
Further it has been stated that the respondent No.7 Samity was 
taking lease from the respondents from time to time. However, on 
20.04.2022 the respondent No.7 obtained lease of Soi Ani Bil Jalmohal 
under Chatmohar Upazilla, Pabna for 1428-1430 B.S. 
On 19.10.2023 the respondent No.2 published a Tender 
Notification being Memo No.05.43.7600.028.40.001.22.2028 inviting 
offers from the aspirant bidders located in different places under District-

<<PAGE 6>>

6
Pabna so far it relates to Kholishagari Jalmohal (Baddho), under 
Chatmohar Upazilla for 1431 B.S. to 1436 B.S. The respondent No.7 as a 
registered Samity made an online application on 13.11.2023 offering lease 
value at Tk. 15,55,000.00/- (Taka fifteen lac and fifty five thousand) 
along with all required documents including a certificate issued by the 
Upazilla Fisheries Officer, Chatmohar, for granting the said lease in its 
favour.  
The respondent No.2 on examining the application so made by the 
respondent No.7 along with all necessary documents granted lease in its 
favour as being the highest bidder vide Memo No.31.00.0000. 
050.68.031.23.119 dated 04.01.2024. Pursuant thereto on 16.01.2024 the 
respondent No.7 paid full amount of the lease money including VAT and 
tax, in total Tk. 19,43,750/- (Taka Nineteen lac forty three thousand and 
seven hundred fifty). 
 Mr. Md. Nurul Islam Sujon, the learned Senior Advocate 
appearing with Mr. Rowshan Alam Khan, the learned Advocate for the 
petitioner categorically submits that  as per clause 2(kha) of the 
Guidelines, 2009 a non-fisherman or a Samity consisting of non-
fishermen members is not eligible to obtain lease of any government 
fishery. In the instant case, he submits, respondent No.2 granted lease in 
favour of the respondent No.7 under development scheme and that some 
of the members of the said samity are not fishermen, as is certified by the 
Upazilla Fishery Officer concerned dated 11.09.2023(Annexure-C1) as 
well as, the report dated 20.02.2024 (Annexure-G of the supplementary 
affidavit to the writ petition) issued by the said authority. Even, the 
Upazilla Fishery Management Committee in its report dated 30.11.2023

<<PAGE 7>>

7
(Annexure-E) had disqualified the respondent No.7 under clause 7(gha) of 
the Guidelines, 2009 on the count “p¢j¢al pLm pcpÉ fÐL«ajvpÉS£h£ eu”. In 
this regard, referring to the said report dated 30.11.2023, the learned 
Counsel goes to contend that said committee concerned had rather 
recommended the petitioner Samity for getting lease of the “Jalmohol” in 
question having fulfilled all requirements of the Guidelines, 2009.Despite 
the same the respondent No.2 has granted lease in favour of the 
respondent No.7, a non-fishermen Samity in flagrant violation of the 
Guidelines, 2009. As such, he submits, the impugned decision of the 
respondent No.2 is liable to be declared to have been passed without 
lawful authority and hence, of no legal effect.     
Mr. Shah Monjurul Hoque, the learned Senior Advocate appearing 
with Mr. Md. Shahinoor Alam, the learned Advocate for the respondent 
No.7 submits that the Tender Notification in question published by the 
respondent No.2 is under development project; as such, said lease matter 
was accordingly dealt with by the committee concerned, which was 
formed pursuant to clause 7(5) of the Guidelines, 2009 and that upon 
scrutinizing the respective documents along with the application filed by 
the respondent No.7 for taking lease of the Jalmohal in question and being 
satisfied with the conditions being fulfilled by the said respondent samity 
the respondent No.2 granted lease in its favour.  
He also goes to contend that fisherman registration for getting 
Fisherman ID Card is a continuous process and that no specific criterion 
has been set out in the Guidelines, 2009 for granting lease under 
development project in respect of registered Fishermen of a samity. 
However, pursuant to Rule 2(Ka) of said Guidelines, “fÐL«a jvpÉS£h£” the

