From a plain reading of the above it appears that the aspirant 
Samity while making application to the authority concerned for lease of 
the respective Jalmohol under development project needs to enclose, 
along with other documents, certificate being certified by the Upazila 
Jalmohal Management Committee that each and every of its members are 
ÒcÖK…Z grm¨RxweÓ. Prior to taking decision thereof by the Ministry concerned 
under Clause 7(5) a report shall be called for, from the concerned Deputy 
Commissioner. The Deputy Commissioner with the assistance of the 
District 
Jalmohal 
Management 
Committee, 
Upazilla 
Jalmohal 
Management Committee, shall scrutinize the information/s /documents 
being supplied by the applicant under clause 7(1) along with the eligibility 
and respective functions of the said Samity. Accordingly, the Deputy 
Commissioner concerned shall forward his opinion along with the report

<<PAGE 12>>

12
to the Ministry concerned for consideration under clause 7(2). On receipt 
thereof being forwarded by the Deputy Commissioner following the 
procedure as provided under Clause 7(1), 7(2), 7(3) and 7(4), the Ministry 
shall forward its decision to the concerned Deputy Commissioner.  
In other words, the report along with the opinion of the Deputy 
Commissioner forwarded under Clause 7(2) is vitally important, basing on 
which the Ministry concerned takes its final decision. 
