In other words, registration and Identification Card are issued to the 
applicant concerned by the authority concerned after due scrutiny under 
the Guidelines, 2019 for identification of the fishermen whose sole 
livelihood is catching fish and selling those in the local market. Despite 
the fact that “plL¡l£ Smjq¡mhÉhÙÛ¡fe¡ e£¢a-2009”  does not prescribe the 
Samity to have members who are required to have registration and 
Identification Card issued under the Guidelines, 2019 but said 
Identification Card, no doubt, plays a vital role for identification of ÒcÖK…Z 
grmRxweÓ.  
In the absence of the said Fishermen Identification Card of all its 
respective members the respondent No.7, however, has failed to produce 
the report and the findings of the concerned Deputy Commissioner so 
have been forwarded to the Ministry concerned under Clause 7(2) to show 
that its respective members are ÒcÖK…Z grm¨RxweÓ, for, basing on the said 
report the Ministry is to give its final decision under Clause 7(5).  
In this regard, it is also pertinent to observe that to that effect this 
Court vide order dated 08.05.2024 gave direction upon the Deputy 
Attorney General of the respondent Government to produce the relevant 
documents for effective disposal of the Rule, but he failed to do so.

<<PAGE 16>>

16
In the absence of the said report and findings of the Deputy 
Commissioner when the respective committee concerned has opined with 
regard to respondent No.7 that “p¢j¢al pLm pcpÉ fËL«a jvpÉS£h£ euz”,  taking 
the impugned decision by the Ministry concerned to grant lease in favour 
of the respondent No.7 cannot be mandated as lawful. 
Accordingly, we find substance in this Rule, though in part. 
In the result, the Rule is made absolute in part. 
The impugned decision of the respondent No.2 dated 04.01.2024 as 
contained in Memo No.31.00.0000.050.68.031.23.119 (Annexure-A) 
granting lease of the fishery in question namely “T.S Case No. 31 i¨š² 
M¡¢mn¡N¡s£ (hÜ) Smjq¡m” under Upazilla-Chatmohar, District-Pabna in 
favour of the respondent No.7, is hereby declared to have been passed 
without lawful authority and hence, of no legal effect. 
Consequently, the lease agreement dated 17.01.2024 (Annexure-
H(A)) so has been executed in between the respondent No.7 and authority 
concerned has lost its force in the eye of law.  
Accordingly, the Ministry concerned is hereby directed to pass its 
respective decision on the lease of the respective ‘Jalmohal’ under clause 
7(5) of the Guidelines, 2009 considering the report of the respective Zilla 
and Upazila Jalmohal Management Committee along with the findings of 
the Deputy Commissioner concerned, in due compliance of law, within a 
period of 2(two) weeks from the date of receipt of the copy of this 
judgment and order.  
In view of the above, the respondent concerned is further directed 
to return the lease money so has been deposited by the respondent No.7

