Montu, B.O","PETITIONER is a cooperative of riparian fishermen which held a government fishery in Pabna on lease for three years and applied for a fresh lease, along with two others. The ministry gave the fishery to another society, relying on a certificate that its members were genuine fishermen, but that society could not produce the identification cards or the deputy commissioner's report on which the guidelines depend. RESPONDENTs are the government and the rival society. The cooperative seeks a declaration against the grant and a direction that the lease be conferred on it instead.","Other: Jalmahal Management Policy, 2009",PARTLY,"The court examined the jalmahal management guidelines and found that the identification of genuine fishermen, whose sole livelihood is catching and selling fish, is central to eligibility, and that the rival society had failed to produce the identification cards of all its members or the report and findings of the deputy commissioner that the guidelines require before the ministry decides. In the absence of that material, and given the committee's own opinion that its members were not genuine fishermen, the grant could not be regarded as lawful. The rule succeeded in part: the grant and the lease agreement were declared to have no lawful basis, and the ministry was directed to decide afresh.",c47d74f2c3e17b451aa335419ca83424d179fe4649aa297066790662a12b9428
