","PETITIONER is the municipality of Narail, which was sued by the district council for an injunction over a beautification project around a public pond, the council claiming a share of the land and objecting to being kept out of the decision. The trial court restrained the municipality and the appellate court confirmed that, and the municipality now says the council has meanwhile floated a tender for a different project on the same land in defiance of the order. RESPONDENT No. 1 is the district council. The municipality seeks reversal of the injunction.","Other: Jilla Parishad Ain, 2000",PARTLY,"The court found that the dispute lay between two local government bodies, that a statute expressly requires any dispute between such bodies to be resolved by the government, the decision of the local government division being final, and that the council had already moved that authority. It held that a quarrel of this kind should not be dragged through the courts. It therefore closed the rule, directed the secretary of the local government division to decide the council's application within two months, kept the status quo over the pond area and the new project until then, but vacated the order relating to the other scheduled land.",61744e1ffccbb0778c1264c2f334e90a6e55702f2317388b67736b669f189f1e
