In an application under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil 
Procedure, 1908 rule was issued calling upon the opposite party No. 1 to 
show cause as to why the order No. 8 dated 08.11.2023 passed by the 
leanred District Judge, Barishal in Miscellaneous Case No. 27 o f 2023 
withdrawing the Title Appeal No. 96 of 2020 from the court of the learned 
Additional District Judge, 1st Court, Barishal and transferring the same to 
the Jananirapatta Bighnakari Aporadh Daman Tribunal, Barishal for 
disposal of the appeal should not be set aside and the Title Appeal No. 96 
of 2020 should not be withdrawn from the court of Jananirapatta 
Bighnakari Aporadh Daman Tribunal, Barishal and should not be 
transferred to any other court and/or pass such other or further order or 
orders as to this court may seem fit and proper. 
   Present  
          Mr. Justice Mamnoon Rahman 
 
 
 
 

<<PAGE 2>>
 
2
The learned Advocate for the opposite party at the very outset 
submits that considering the delay in the disposal of the Title Appeal being 
No. 96 of 2020 she has no objection if the Title Appeal be transferred to 
any other court for quick disposal. 
The learned Advocate for the petitioner concedes to the prayer. 
I have heard the learned Advocates for the petitioner as well as 
opposite party. I have perused the impugned judgment and order passed by 
the court below, rule issuing order, revisional application, grounds taken 
thereon as well as necessary papers and documents annexed herewith. 
Considering the facts and circumstances, I am inclined to transfer the 
case to any other court only considering the quick disposal of the appeal. 
Accordingly, let the Title Appeal being No. 96 of 2020 be withdrawn from 
the court of Jananirapatta Bighnakari Aporadh Daman Tribunal, Barishal 
and be transferred to the court of learned District Judge, Barishal forthwith. 
The court below is directed to hear and dispose of the same strictly on 
merit by applying its independent and judicial mind expeditiously, as 
possible, not later than 3(three) months from the date of receipt of the 
instant order without fail and without giving any adjournment to the 
parties. However, this order shall not affect the disposal of the appeal on 
merit.  
With this observation and direction, the instant rule is disposed of. 
The office is directed to communicate the judgment and order to the 
concerned court blow, at once.  
           
 
           
 
 
