","PETITIONER was convicted by an Additional Sessions Judge at Chapainawabganj in 2019 under section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act and sentenced to a year's imprisonment and a fine of fourteen lakh taka, over a cheque for thirteen lakh fifty-three thousand taka drawn on the same bank branch as in the companion appeal, dishonoured for insufficient funds. A legal notice was sent and ignored and the complaint was filed within the statutory period. RESPONDENTs are the state and the payee. He appeals against the conviction and sentence, contending that the offence was not established, though nobody appeared on his side at the hearing.","Other: Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",REFUSED,"The court reviewed the record and found that the payee had proved the cheque, the dishonour slip, the notice with its postal receipt and the complaint, that the notice was despatched within the period the statute allows and the case brought in time, and that all the ingredients of the offence were satisfied. It found the trial judge to have taken the material aspects into account and to have reached a correct conclusion, leaving no room for interference. The appeal accordingly failed, the conviction and sentence were affirmed, bail was recalled and the deposit made at filing was released to the complainant.",d297136809c5ff5624a75139288dc40cf3f7d1693828bd55c27b574886d1197f
