                                                  I agree.","PETITIONERs are children of nationally recognised freedom fighters and an association formed by them, who moved this court under Article 102 against a circular of 2018 that stopped reserving posts in the public services for their class. They say the circular defeats the Appellate Division's affirmation of the earlier direction that thirty per cent of posts be reserved for such children and that the words permitting an unfilled reserved post to be kept vacant be struck out. RESPONDENTs are the government and the concerned board. The petitioners seek a declaration that the circular is without lawful authority.","Constitution of Bangladesh, Article 102",ALLOWED,"The court held that the Appellate Division had already settled the question, upholding the reservation of thirty per cent of posts for children of freedom fighters and expunging the words that would have kept an unfilled reserved post vacant, and that this was binding on every authority under the Constitution. It found the circular of 2018 to be in plain disregard of that decision, of the earlier office order and of the rights of that class. The rule therefore succeeded: the circular was declared unlawful and of no legal effect, and the authorities were directed to restore the reservation, along with those for districts, women, the disabled and ethnic groups, by notification within three months.",fae42eaba14bd35a4498e3b0ecdbf1c7eda13903ed5f4d4d94dd22f23ad754f7
