From the above, it appears that (a) an assessee in his discretion 
may engage an Authorized Representative (AR) to represent him who may 
or may not be a new tax payer;  
(b) An AR is entitled to represent an assessee in connection with the 
proceedings under the Ain, 2023 before the concerned tax Authority or 
the Tribunal, as the case may be;  
(c) An AR is entitled to prepare and furnish revised return in 
addition to original return;  
(d) An AR is entitled to charge his professional fees from the 
respective tax payer for rendering his respective service(s);  
(e) An AR is entitled to file return of the respective assessee both 
manually as well as by using online platform.  
Keeping in view of the purpose/object of the Ain, 2023 to collect 
lawful tax even from those who remain outside the domain of tax net as 
well as to expand the area of imposition of tax for the revenue interest of 
the country and also, through the assistance of TRP to approach the 
persons concerned who have TIN certificate and have taxable income and 
to motivate as well as to assist them to prepare and furnish return of 
income through online platform the NBR in exercise of power as provided 
under Section 343 framed Rules, 2023 and thereby has introduced a class 
of persons under the name and style “Tax Return Preparer”. Said TRP 
having required qualifications as provided under Rule 3 is certified by the 
NBR subject to passing the Tax Aptitude and Accounting Test  (TAAT) 

