","PETITIONER is a member of a school and college at Sujanagar, Pabna, who moved this court after the education board, instead of approving the governing body that had been constituted in observance of the required formalities, constituted an ad hoc committee by an office order of 2022. He also sought a direction on his pending application of December 2021. RESPONDENTs are the chairman of the Rajshahi education board and others. The petitioner seeks a declaration that the office order constituting the ad hoc committee is without lawful authority and of no legal effect.","Other: Intermediate and Secondary Education Ordinance, 1961",PARTLY,"The court found that by the time the petition came up for hearing the tenure of the ad hoc committee had expired and so had the tenure of the governing body it had replaced, so that the challenge had been overtaken by events and no declaration could usefully be made. It held that a regular governing body must in any event be constituted by a free and fair election, and that with no governing body in place the board was the appropriate authority to arrange it. The rule was accordingly disposed of with a direction on the board to constitute a fresh ad hoc committee within one month for holding the election.",1068100b1e6298193a76e783e2ac4b705abbee3a323f54aa015ac6ff201c83c6
