Asad/B.O","PETITIONERs are co-sharers of land in a municipal area which the education ministry wanted acquired for a school, directing the authorities in 2017 to complete the acquisition by paying adequate compensation on an urgent basis. Notices were issued under the acquisition statute and a joint inquiry was held, which recommended that part of the land, described as fallow, be treated as paddy land, and the category of the land was then changed to the disadvantage of the owners. RESPONDENTs are the government and the acquiring officer. The petitioners seek a declaration that the notices in the wrong name and the change of category are without lawful authority.","Other: Acquisition and Requisition of Immovable Property Act, 2017",ALLOWED,"The court examined the inquiry report, the municipal rent receipts and the government's own instructions on land development tax, and found that the disputed portion had remained fallow and was not used for cultivation, that development tax was being collected at the rate applicable to residential land, and that the committee's recommendation to treat it as paddy land was a mere recommendation never carried into the record. It held that the owner was entitled to compensation on the footing of residential land. The rule therefore succeeded, and the authorities were directed to issue fresh notices within sixty days showing the current date and the correct category of the land.",b0309d23e02d6b6ebcf0ae87ad6aa663ecde451db557053001b0bb1828035784
